        {
          "path": "_m/k/e/7/f/orlando-power-station-wp/colourful-cooling-towers-of-th.jpg",
          "filename": "Colourful cooling towers of the decommisioned Orlando Power Station (4612453602).jpg",
          "caption": "Orlando Power Station is a decommissioned coal fired power station in Soweto, South Africa. The power station was commissioned at the end of the Second World War and served Johannesburg  for over 50 years.\nThe two cooling towers are a prominent landmark in Soweto. They were build in 1951 to replace the spray pond cooling system used up to that tim\nBeing supplied by sewage effluent from the Klipspruit Sewage Works, the spray ponds at Orlando were the first in South Africa to make use of this ready supply of coolant liquid.\n\nBoth towers are painted, one functioning as an advertising billboard and the other containing the largest mural painting in South Africa. The towers are also used for bungee and BASE jumping from a platform between the top of the two towers as well as a bungee swing into one of the towers.[Wikipedia.org]",
          "alt": "Orlando Power Station is a decommissioned coal fired power station in Soweto, South Africa. The power station was commissioned at the end of the Second World War and served Johannesburg  for over 50 years.\nThe two cooling towers are a prominent landmark in Soweto. They were build in 1951 to replace the spray pond cooling system used up to that tim\nBeing supplied by sewage effluent from the Klipspruit Sewage Works, the spray ponds at Orlando were the first in South Africa to make use of this ready supply of coolant liquid.\n\nBoth towers are painted, one functioning as an advertising billboard and the other containing the largest mural painting in South Africa. The towers are also used for bungee and BASE jumping from a platform between the top of the two towers as well as a bungee swing into one of the towers.[Wikipedia.org]",
          "width": 1625,
          "height": 1172,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Jorge Láscar from Australia",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colourful_cooling_towers_of_the_decommisioned_Orlando_Power_Station_(4612453602).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "orlando-power-station-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "ke7f",
